    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d624">

                <pb facs="0683" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg675"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.60C/94: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-16T09:00:00+03:00">September 16, 1939—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 19—12:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>201. Following from Biddle.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“6, September 15, 11 p.m.</p>
                    <p>1. Considering it more suitable under circumstances Beck decided remove his
                        headquarters to Stavekuty<anchor n="14" xml:id="d624-f1"/> and requested
                        mission chiefs to maintain contact with him there. At the same time Beck
                        specially urged me to set up means of continuous communication with my
                        Government. Accordingly pursuant my today’s request our Minister in
                        Bucharest (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) is sending Misses McQuatters and
                        Saunders to Cerneuerti [<hi rendition="#italic">Cernauti</hi>]<anchor n="15"
                            xml:id="d624-f2"/> where (subject to your approval) I consider essential
                        establishing a relay communications bureau at Black Eagle Hotel and (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">b</hi>) is retaining also subject to your approval
                        Misses Hillery and Pinard to assist relaying messages between Bucharest and
                        Department.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d624-f1" n="14" xml:id="d624-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably staff headquarters temporarily at Kuty, in southeastern Poland, near
                    Rumanian frontier (Bukovina).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d624-f2" n="15" xml:id="d624-f2-content">
                <p>In northern Rumania, near Polish frontier.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
